---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<div class="container">
		<header>
			<h1>Tools</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">
				Curated tools to speed up daily work.
			</p>
		</header>

		<h2>Session managment</h2>

		<p>Make sure you have shit+enter configured to go to a new line (setup instructions) (/terminal-setup)</p>
		<p>Check your usage (claude /usage, same for copilot)</p>
		<p>Check your current context usage (claude /context, same for copilot)</p>
		<p>Clear your context / start a new session (claude /clear, same for copilot)</p>
		<p>How to interrupt the current (claude ctrl+c or ESC, same for copilot)</p>

		<h2>Prompting</h2>

		<p>Referenceing specific files, use the @ symbol, then select the file with up and down error. These files will be added to your context. (same for copilot)</p>

		<p>You can stash a command with ctrl+s. After the next command you get your stased command back. (does not exist in copilot)</p>

		<p>Copy & Paste images into the CLI. Does not work in WSL. (needs checking, on native)</p>

		<h2>GHCP Cli and VSCode</h2>

		<p>Connect to your IDE via /ide. This allows you to view diffs directly in your IDE, rather than a regular diff in the terminal (/ide, same for GHCP CLI)</p>


		<h2>Time travel</h2>

		<p>ESC + ESC to enter the time travel mode. Now you can select where to go and how to go there,
			Restore code and conversation, Restore conversation (code will be unchanged), Restore code (conversation will be unchanged). (same in GHCP without the options, /undo /rewind)</p>

		<p>Resuming sessions - exit claude code and resume by running `claude --resume <session-id>` (same for GHCP CLI)</p>
		<p>Can not remember your session id? `claude --continue` (same for GHCP CLI)</p>
		<p>Start claude without parameters, /resume (same for GHCP CLI)</p>

		<h2>Bash commands?!</h2>
		<p>Running a shell command - ! to enter the bash mode. CTRL+B to run a command (like a dev server in the background). Arrow keys to get back to that background session (GHCP CLI ! to enter shell mode, no way to return to running processes?! needs investigation)</p>

		<p>CTRL + Z + fg</p>

		<h2>Permissions</h2>

		<p>Permissions are stored in .claude/settings.local.json (GHCP CLI ~/.copilot/permissions-config.json)</p>
		<p>Permissions can be shared in a team with .claude/settings.json (GHCP CLI does not support this)</p>

		<p>Sources:<br />
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/use-copilot-cli-agents/overview#further-reading">Using GHCP CLI</a><br />
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/cli-best-practices#6-advanced-patterns">Advanced Patterns</a><br />
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/copilot-cli-reference/cli-command-reference">slash commands</a>
		</p>

	</div>
	<div class="container">
		<header>
			<h1>GHCP Fundamentals</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">
				Constraints of LLMs
			</p>
		</header>
		<h2>Smart zone vs Dumb zone</h2>
		<p> 80-100k Token<br />
				Sources: 
				- https://medium.com/@rajesh.godavarthi/context-engineering-what-ai-builders-know-that-you-dont-5-counter-intuitive-lessons-from-the-8435308183ca
				- https://www.tqdev.com/2025-context-engineering-mastering-ai-tools/
		1m Tokens = more dumb zone
		</p>

		<h2>Training data cut off</h2>
		<h2>No memory / stateless</h2>
	</div>
	<div class="container">
		<header>
			<h1>GHCP Fundamentals</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">
				 What are subagents
			</p>
		</header>
		<h2>Orchestrator</h2>
		<p>Orchestrator spwans multiple sub agents

			- used to save context in the orchestrator
			- can be spwaned with different model
			- can be spwaned with different system prompt
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="container">
		<header>
			<h1>GHCP Fundamentals</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">
				 Codebase Exploration
			</p>
		</header>
		<h2>Problem</h2>
		<p>Whenever the agent does something it has to explore the codebase (stateless). <br />
			Being able to explore the codebase is crucial since you do it basically every time you start a new session.
			<br />
			Prompt: "What is the tech stack of this codebase and what is its purpose?<br />
			Prompt: "Explore the codebase and tell me the tech stack of this codebase and what is its purpose?<br />
		</p>
		<h2>Showing context</h2>
		<h2>What is plan mode?</h2>
		<p>- new system prompt, only read, bash and MCP Servers
			- interrogate me about every single design decision inside here so that we both understand what we're trying to build better
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
